Subject: [PATCH] 5285: the language the owner chose in the app answers their
 own line
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Lika №27: English chosen on her profile, an English question, a Georgian reply
— her other conversations outvoted the line in front of the run. The app sends
the chosen language as X-Locale on every request; the send route now passes it
to the run, and it decides when the owner's line carries no language or the
same one. A line written in another language still decides for itself, and a
language asked for in words (D752) still wins. Engine wakes are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
